## Why This Is Asked
Assesses end-to-end TLS termination, dynamic cert provisioning, and zero-downtime reload in a Podman-based RH9 setup. Also tests firewall (nftables), SELinux, and service upgrade discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Podman, nginx as TLS terminator, Vault integration, in-container watcher, systemd upgrades, nftables, SELinux, SNI routing

## Code Example
```nginx
# tls_preread for SNI, per-tenant certs loaded from /etc/nginx/certs
stream {
  map $ssl_preread_server_name $tenant {
    tenantA backendA;
    tenantB backendB;
    tenantC backendC;
  }
  server {
    listen 8443;
    ssl_preread on;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle Vault outage and certificate revocation?
- How to validate zero-downtime during upgrades?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to build a multi-tenant TLS termination with live updates in a containerized RH9 setup, including security and networking constraints.

## Key Concepts
- TLS with SNI and per-tenant certs
- Podman container networking
- Local CA management and cert rotation
- systemd-based zero-downtime reloads
- SELinux policy and nftables isolation
- End-to-end test planning

## Code Example
```javascript
// watcher: rotate tenant certs and reload proxy
const fs = require('fs');
const { execSync } = require('child_process');
const watchDir = '/var/lib/proxy/certs';
const watcher = require('chokidar').watch(watchDir);
watcher.on('change', (path) => {
  if (path.endsWith('.pem')) {
    fs.copyFileSync(`${watchDir}/current.pem`, '/var/run/proxy/current.pem.bak');
    execSync('systemctl reload rhproxy');
  }
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you revoke a tenant cert without downtime?
- How would you validate multi-tenant isolation under load?
